--- !u!114 &114340500867371532
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01270efd3285ea4a9d6c555cb0a8027, type: 3}
  m_Name: VFXUI
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  groupInfos:
  - title: Alpha from distance to center
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 1129
      y: 2199
      width: 1291
      height: 574
    contents: []
  stickyNoteInfos:
  - title: Axis calculations
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 2218
      y: 637
      width: 357
      height: 100
    contents: 'As the vortex center is at position(0,0,0) in Local space, we don''t
      have to calculate the particlepos-vortexpos vector because it is equivalent
      to the particlepos (X-0=X)

      So the CrossProduct between particlepos and
      Z vector gives us the vector used as force direction for orbital behaviour'
    theme: 
    textSize: Small
    colorTheme: 1
  - title: Greyscale
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 2107
      y: 1933
      width: 252
      height: 100
    contents: When wanting a greyscale, color value can be set using a float. A random
      number is easier to use to set random colors in that case
    theme: 
    textSize: Small
    colorTheme: 1
  - title: Premultiplied
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 2516
      y: 1975
      width: 184
      height: 100
    contents: "In premultiplied blend mode, \nAlpha = Alpha\nColor = Color*Alpha"
    theme: 
    textSize: Small
    colorTheme: 1
  - title: Sphere collision
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 3261
      y: 1239
      width: 217
      height: 100
    contents: This allows to make sure that the smoke will stay forever in the portal
      range, as turbulence and other forces blocks could drag it away with time.
    theme: 
    textSize: Small
    colorTheme: 1
  - title: Six way smoke lit
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 3277.155
      y: 1569.8075
      width: 211
      height: 100
    contents: 'Six way smoke lighting is available for LIT outputs by changing the
      material type in the output''s inspector. '
    theme: 
    textSize: Small
    colorTheme: 1
  categories: []
  uiBounds:
    serializedVersion: 2
    x: 1129
    y: -693
    width: 2359
    height: 3466
